meta {
  name: 9. Set Field Value On Task
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/projects/items/{{taskId}}/fields
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "values": [
      { "templateItemId": {{taskDescriptionFieldId}}, "value": "Set from Bruno" }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  taskDescriptionFieldId is captured by the previous request ("8. Get Field Values"). The next request
  ("10. Delete", which cascades onto this task) exercises the ItemFieldValue cleanup on cascading item
  delete.

  Try a templateItemId that belongs to a different template (e.g. the Feature template's id from
  "Templates/1. Get Global") to see it rejected with "... does not belong to this item's template".
}
